            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to hum a tune, then the Kannada for to play an instrument."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ವಾದ್ಯ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವಾದ್ಯ — vādya — \"a musical instrument\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮದುವೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ವಾದ್ಯಗಳ ಸದ್ದು ಜೋರಾಗಿತ್ತು. maduveyalli vādyagaḷa saddu jōrāgittu. At the wedding the instruments were loud."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ವಾದ್ಯಗಳು, vādyagaḷu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವಾದ್ಯಗಾರ, a player."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವಾದ್ಯ (vādya) is borrowed from Sanskrit vādya, \"to be played; music, a musical instrument\" (CDIAL 11511)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
